From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 22:40:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: recompute AP TPC after channel changes

num_pwr_levels is also populated by the local TPC calculation. On an AP,
reusing that output as evidence of a received TPE selects zeroed TPE
limits on the next vdev restart. A 6 GHz 160/320 MHz CSA then lowers
the reported power to 0 dBm and reduces the client signal.

Only stations receive a TPE from an AP. Recompute an AP power table
from the current channel definition after each restart, including its
new bandwidth, instead of reusing the previous output level count.
Keep the existing station TPE handling unchanged.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -12318,7 +12318,12 @@
 	start_freq = ath12k_mac_get_6ghz_start_frequency(&ctx->def);
 	pwr_reduction = bss_conf->pwr_reduction;
 
-	if (arvif->reg_tpc_info.num_pwr_levels) {
+	/* Only a station can have a received TPE. AP num_pwr_levels is
+	 * cached output from the previous TPC calculation, not a TPE.
+	 * Recompute it for the new channel width after a restart/CSA.
+	 */
+	if (ahvif->vdev_type == WMI_VDEV_TYPE_STA &&
+	    reg_tpc_info->num_pwr_levels) {
 		is_tpe_present = true;
 		num_pwr_levels = arvif->reg_tpc_info.num_pwr_levels;
 	} else {
